## The final turn — at {FINAL_TURN_AT} (stop-at minus 20 minutes)

**Stop verifying.** Anything unverified at this moment is reported as unverified; you do not
trade the handoff for one more check. Write, in this order:

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `runs/run-{NN}/REPORT.md` | what shipped. **Every number re-read from the artifact right now.** Unpushed-commit counts re-derived, never carried. |
| `runs/run-{NN}/OWNER-QUESTIONS.md` | decisions needed, each with the options and your recommendation, ending in a blank `## RULINGS` section for the owner |
| `runs/run-{NN}/HANDOFF.md` | gotchas + **what was verified** — the next run MUST NOT re-verify it |
| `runs/run-{NN}/next-shift/RUN.md` | proposed shape + theme + MUST-MEET legs for the **{NEXT_SHIFT}** run |
| `runs/run-{NN}/next-shift/PROMPTS.md` | paste-ready prompts for that run, one section per lane |

The owner's check-in reads `REPORT.md` -> `OWNER-QUESTIONS.md` -> `next-shift/PROMPTS.md`.
Review, feedback, paste. Write for that ritual and nothing else.

Then run the closer (PS 5.1-safe, no `&&`):

```powershell
{CLOSE_RUN_PS1} -RunDir '{RUN_DIR}' -RepoPath '{REPO_PATH}' -CloseSha '<the named commit>'
```

It tags `run-{NN}-close`, flips the LEDGER row, deletes scratch and verifies the deletion, and
emits `CONFORMANCE.json`.

